an once at this stage. "],["pg",""],["ls","nd"],["ls","sd"],["hs","nc"],["hs","sc"],["at","Suppose South crosses in clubs "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["ls","sc"],["pc","c"],["pc","c"],["pc","ca"],["pc","c"],["pg",""],["hs","nd"],["hs","sd"],["at","to take two diamond finesses. "],["pg",""],["ls","nd"],["ls","Sd"],["pc","d9"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","dq"],["hs","eh"],["at","Both finesses win, but when East discards on the second round of diamonds, "],["pg",""],["ls","eh"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hs","wd"],["at","West's remaining diamonds stop the suit and there is no way for South to come to 12 tricks. "],["pg",""],["up","8"],["hs","wc"],["nt","When West was dealt 4 (or more) diamonds to the @DK, South's only chance is to hope that West was also dealt the sole defensive club guard. If this is the case then it is possible to ^*Bsqueeze^*N West for a 12th trick. "],["pg",""],["ls","wc"],["ls","wd"],["nt","South takes the first diamond finesse, running the @D9."],["pc","d9"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["at"," When the first finesse succeeds, that is a good sign!"],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["ls","wc"],["hs","ns"],["hs","ss"],["at"," In order for the squeeze to mature it is necessary to run the spades before taking the second diamond finesse. "],["pg",""],["hs","ns"],["hs","ss"],["ls","ns"],["ls","ss"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pc","sk"],["pc","s"],["pg",""],["pc","sj"],["pc","s"],["pc","sq"],["pc","s"],["pg",""],["pc","sa"],["pc","h"],["pc","c"],["pc","s"],["pg",""],["pc","s"],["pc","c"],["pc","d"],["pc","s"],["pg",""],["hs","sh"],["at","When South plays the @HQ, "],["pg",""],["ls","sh"],["pc","h"],["hs","wd"],["hs","wc"],["at","West is squeezed in the minors. "],["pg",""],["ls","wc"],["nt","If West discards a diamond, "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hs","nd"],["hs","sd"],["at","South will be able to run the diamond suit after taking a second finesse. "],["pg",""],["up","3"],["ls","nd"],["ls","sd"],["hs","wc"],["at","If, instead of a diamond, West discards a club on the @HQ, "],["pg",""],["ls","sc"],["ls","wc"],["pc","c"],["pc","d"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hs","sc"],["hs","wd"],["at","South's clubs will run and it won't matter how many diamonds West was dealt (as long as he was dealt the @DK). "],["pg",""],["up","28"],["ls","sc"],["ls","wd"],["nt","Many players consider the squeeze to be a technique used only by experts. As this deal illustrates, executing a squeeze sometimes involves little more than declarer playing his winners in the proper order. "],["pg",""],["hs","nd"],["hs","sd"],["at","All basic squeeze positions require an entry to the hand opposite the last side suit winners (South's hearts and spades in this deal). Playing a second round of diamonds too early in the play destroys this entry, making it impossible for the squeeze to succeed."],["",""]]}}